  "name": "AMOEBIC SEROLOGY",
  "code": "AMOEB-001",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"626\" data-end=\"706\">\n<p data-start=\"628\" data-end=\"706\">Amoebic serology detects <strong data-start=\"653\" data-end=\"671\">IgG antibodies</strong> against <em data-start=\"680\" data-end=\"703\">Entamoeba histolytica</em>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"707\" data-end=\"831\">\n<p data-start=\"709\" data-end=\"831\">Useful in diagnosing <strong data-start=\"730\" data-end=\"761\">extra-intestinal amoebiasis</strong> (especially liver abscess), since stool microscopy may be negative.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"832\" data-end=\"1168\">\n<p data-start=\"834\" data-end=\"852\"><strong data-start=\"834\" data-end=\"850\">Limitations:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"855\" data-end=\"1168\">\n<li data-start=\"855\" data-end=\"968\">\n<p data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"968\">Antibodies may persist for <strong data-start=\"884\" data-end=\"903\">months to years</strong>, so a positive result does <strong data-start=\"931\" data-end=\"965\">not always mean active disease</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"971\" data-end=\"1045\">\n<p data-start=\"973\" data-end=\"1045\">Cannot distinguish between <strong data-start=\"1000\" data-end=\"1017\">past exposure</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1022\" data-end=\"1042\">active infection</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1048\" data-end=\"1168\">\n<p data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1168\">Should be interpreted with <strong data-start=\"1077\" data-end=\"1165\">clinical findings, imaging (USG/CT for liver abscess), and stool antigen tests / PCR</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1263\">\n<p data-start=\"1171\" data-end=\"1263\"><strong data-start=\"1171\" data-end=\"1190\">Negative result</strong> does not exclude intestinal amoebiasis, especially early in infection.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
